message:
Order volume is below its usual range for this hour and day of week.

This is browser-measured and directional, so confirm against the platform's own order report before treating it as an outage. Start with the RUM dashboard: is revenue down with it, are checkout errors up, did a deploy land?

{{#is_alert}}Check the checkout funnel and recent deploys.{{/is_alert}}
{{#is_recovery}}Order volume is back in range.{{/is_recovery}}

Revenue is below its usual range for this hour and day of week.

Revenue is reported in the store currency with no conversion, so scope this monitor by `currency` if the store sells in more than one.

{{#is_alert}}Compare with order volume: a revenue drop without an order drop points at average order value, not at checkout breaking.{{/is_alert}}

Fewer than 20% of started checkouts became orders in the last hour.

Set the threshold from this store's own baseline: 20% is a placeholder, not a benchmark. Pull a week of `rum.commerce.orders / rum.commerce.checkouts_started` first and set the critical threshold below the normal floor.

{{#is_alert}}Look at checkout errors and checkout view INP in the same window.{{/is_alert}}

Errors on pages carrying commerce context are elevated.

Set the threshold from this store's own error floor; 50 in 15 minutes is a placeholder.

{{#is_alert}}Open Error Tracking filtered to `@context.commerce.platform:*`, then watch whether order volume follows.{{/is_alert}}
